notes={
 'W10-P01':('Make the two 200-point performances personally different, not two generic conquerors.','Retain both canonical characters and their separate Week 10 story contexts.','His Majesty’s Blood’s gift and The LLC’s command chair supply two distinct character signatures in one editorial cover. Do not convert the title into a literal roof breaking.','No invented meeting, 200-inscribed title belt, or replacement identity.','facts.json#/history_200'),
 'W10-P02':('Let the opening connect the issue’s shared pressure without replaying every payoff.','Keep the published briefing table, map, banner and folio language and full current narration.','Use the already specified scene props as connective clues. The table should lead into the six events rather than look like a fixture list pasted over a landscape.','No new map borders, scene teleportation, duplicated opening headline or silent prose cuts.','issue-previs.json#W10-P02'),
 'W10-P03':('Address the league as people who will remember the week, not as a production-system report.','Keep the distinction between fictional consequences and the actual standings.','Let the shared birthday, broken hoop and passing truck examples carry the voice. Keep the institutional scene restrained and the entire address readable.','No invented commissioner portrait, real quote, or claims that story outcomes change league rules.','issue-previs.json#W10-P03'),
 'W10-P04':('Make the six exact results the neutral reference point for the stories.','Keep all six pairings, full names and final figures in their current order.','Use consistent winning/losing emphasis and generous row spacing, not an enlarged favorite matchup that hides another result.','No re-sorting pairings, obsolete live scores or ornate perspective distorting digits.','facts.json#/games'),
 'W10-P11':('Give the audience a breath and show that one world receives different weather.','Keep the established regional sequence and routes.','Use coast, inland wind and delayed wetland runoff as spatial continuity. Reduce the title’s dominance so the landscape, not another poster frame, supplies the transition.','No new geography, literal division borders, or principal-character cameos.','issue-previs.json#W10-P11'),
 'W10-P18':('Explain which managers benefited from actual player contributions without hindsight shaming.','Keep the six category leaders, the two three-player totals and the non-scoring bench distinction.','Let the final Monday contribution give ObiWan Jacoby’s resistance factual context; distinguish strong scoring in defeat from a failed effort.','No bench points added to a score, optimal-lineup claims or inferred manager motives.','facts.json#/derived'),
 'W10-P34':('Make consequences useful to the affected managers without making injuries a joke.','Keep the exact dates, qualified diagnoses, indirect D/ST exposure and current roster joins.','Differentiate newly reported issues from retained absences with typography and dispatch grouping rather than a dramatic medical illustration.','No upgraded diagnosis, guaranteed return, medical joke, or personal-health inference about an owner.','sports-news-pass3.json'),
 'W10-P25':('Present practical preparation, not blame for a still-editable future lineup.','Keep the current seven uncovered specialist positions across six teams.','Organize each team and its need as one readable unit in the loggia. Show absence through logistics and empty hooks, not invented injured character bodies.','No assumed acquisition, player assignment, finished Week 11 lineup or stale Monday starter replay.','facts.json#/pass3/readiness'),
 'W10-P26':('Let the actual transaction trail reveal human choices without inventing intent.','Keep the completed-event window, exact FAAB, dates and owner changes.','The Mason trail, Brian Thomas Jr. move and receiver claims should remain distinct chronological stories; make the source order clear inside one intake scene.','No failed claim called a completed move, add/drop called a trade, or invented reason for an owner’s action.','facts.json#/completed_transactions'),
 'W10-P27':('Show why equal records still feel different to different owners.','Preserve all twelve official rows and the posted seed order.','Emphasize the six-team 6–4 cluster and the cutoff without moving rows or turning points-for order into seeding. Keep the hall secondary to comparison.','No creative seed reorder, invented tiebreak rule or visual omission of bottom teams.','final-league-snapshot.json#/standings'),
 'W10-P28':('Make the three division situations distinct without inventing three countries.','Retain Burgers, Pizza and Wings membership and current records.','Let the three standards share one terrace, with each pressure paragraph adjacent to its correct emblem in a level editorial plane.','No literal borders, new titles or implied automatic playoff qualification.','facts.json#/divisions'),
 'W10-P29':('Explain scoring form as a different lens from the official standings.','Keep all twelve rows, final input scope and the unchanged 70/30 formula.','Use the lake/bridge landscape as a calm counterpoint; make the method visible before the reader mistakes the order for playoff seeds.','No stealth injury adjustment, invented probability or changed weight.','facts.json#/scoring_form'),
 'W10-P30':('Make remaining possibility visible without pretending every route is equally likely.','Keep seven berths, four games and the verified Mud Dogs next-loss condition.','Let the climb carry the time sequence. Keep explanatory text level in calm spaces and the harsh specific condition near the relevant note.','No invented odds, automatic clinches, or promoting a mathematical witness into a prediction.','playoff-witnesses-final.json'),
 'W10-P31':('Answer why every Week 11 fixture matters, not just who plays.','Keep all six away-at-home pairings and their checked implication fields.','Attach each stake immediately to its fixture. Give head-to-head and the three divisional rounds one clear closing place; avoid a duplicated summary beneath a large list.','No automatic-elimination label for The LLC or other bubble teams when a qualifying counterexample exists; do not omit Mud Dogs.','production-evidence/finalization-20261117/USER_WEEK11_FOLIO_ADDITION.md'),
 'W10-P35':('Turn the two contenders’ known history into anticipation, not an early result.','Keep His Majesty’s Blood and the four-legged D0nkey K0ng on opposing bridge approaches with open space between them.','Let posture and distance carry the rivalry; the older 179.68–111.42 receipt remains explicitly historical and the present 6–4 records distinct.','No first strike, future winner, title transfer, wrong centaur anatomy or old score presented as Week 11.','facts.json#/pass3/week11_gotw'),
 'W10-P33':('End on the delivery winner preparing to become next week’s host.','Keep Slob on my Dobb at the known foothill shelter with secured kegs and incoming weather.','Use calm preparation as the contrast to the noisy issue. The weather previews El Niño; the final paragraph should land in the shelter’s light, not another detached black box.','No unbound second character, finished future game or assertion that a future win caused the present storm.','issue-previs.json#W10-P33')}
